{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.064,
            0.378,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.12,
            0.886,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "the square along this line, the points B, C on the right get reflected to the left side and occupy the positions occupied earlier by A, D. What happens to the points A, D? A occupies the position occupied by B and D that of C!"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.228,
            0.617,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.408,
            0.886,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "What if we reflect along the diagonal from A to C? Where do points A, B, C and D go? What if we reflect along the horizontal line of symmetry?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.477,
            0.884,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "A figure that has a line or lines of symmetry is thus, also said to have **reflection symmetry**."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.539,
            0.707,
            0.562
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Generating shapes having lines of symmetry"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.568,
            0.885,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": "So far we have seen symmetrical figures and asymmetrical figures. How does one generate such symmetrical figures? Let us explore this."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.642,
            0.339,
            0.662
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ink Blot Devils"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.665,
            0.885,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "You enjoyed doing this earlier in Class 5. Take a piece of paper. Fold it in half. Open the paper and spill a few drops of ink (or paint) on one half."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.734,
            0.854,
            0.756
          ],
          "content": "Now press the halves together and then open the paper again."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.757,
            0.416,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "• What do you see?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.779,
            0.586,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": "• Is the resulting figure symmetric?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.802,
            0.624,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": "If yes, where is the line of symmetry?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.824,
            0.884,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": "Is there any other line along which it can be folded to produce two identical parts?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.871,
            0.567,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": "• Try making more such patterns."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.942,
            0.115,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
